Remove the howdy-gtk front-end from the build. Void ships no python
'elevate' module, so howdy-gtk cannot run; the core PAM module and CLI
do not depend on it (compare.py launches it only if present and
swallows the missing-binary error).

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 65a5bc6..f8ed5ac 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -17,5 +17,4 @@ paths_dict = {
 }
 
 # We need to keep this order beause howdy-gtk defines the gtk script path which is used later in howdy
-subdir('howdy-gtk')
 subdir('howdy')
\ No newline at end of file
